Translator's note

6
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Translator's note

7
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Now we were talking about the necessity

8
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,000
of human beings changing,

9
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,000
and why they don't change,

10
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,500
why they accept these

11
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:32,000
intolerable conditions of human psyche.

12
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:36,000
I think we ought to go

13
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:41,000
or approach the same thing from a different angle.

14
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Who has invented this unconscious?

15
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Who has invented it?

16
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:01,000
I think the unconscious,

17
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:04,000
there's a difference between what we call the unconscious

18
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:06,000
and what is the unconscious.

19
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,000
The word is not the thing.

20
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Yes, the word is not the thing.

21
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Who has thought it up?

22
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,500
Well, I think the history

23
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:19,000
of the thinking about the unconscious

24
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:23,000
is a long and involved process.

25
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,000
I think it began

26
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:26,000
in the early 20th century.

27
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:29,000
May we ask, have you an unconscious?

28
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Again, we're into a language problem.

29
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Have I an unconscious?

30
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:39,000
Are you aware of your unconscious?

31
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Do you know you have an unconscious

32
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:46,000
that is operating differently

33
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,000
or trying to give you hints?

34
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:50,000
You know, all that.

35
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Are you aware of all that?

36
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Yes.

37
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:54,000
I am aware,

38
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:59,000
of an aspect of myself

39
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,000
that I look at it a little differently.

40
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,000
I look at it that there's an aspect of myself

41
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:07,000
that is aware incompletely.

42
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,000
That's what I call the unconscious.

43
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:13,000
It is aware of my experience

44
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,000
or aware of the events

45
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:17,000
in an incomplete way.

46
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,000
That's what I call the unconscious.

47
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Now, it uses symbols

48
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,000
and different modes of telling me,

49
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,000
of understanding.

50
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:29,000
In other words, a dream

51
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:34,000
where I am discovering jealousy

52
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,000
in the dream, right?

53
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,000
That I wasn't aware of.

54
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:42,000
But would you also give importance

55
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,000
or were you, Dr. Bohm,

56
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,000
a feeling that there is such a thing?

57
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,000
Well, I don't know what we mean by that.

58
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:50,000
I think we can...

59
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:53,000
The phenomena are that there are some things we do

60
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:55,000
whose origin we're not aware of.

61
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:57,000
You see, we react,

62
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:02,000
we use words in a habitual way.

63
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,000
We have dreams.

64
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:05,000
We have dreams.

65
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:06,000
I mean, I suppose we...

66
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,000
I'm going to question all that,

67
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:09,000
because I am not sure...

68
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:12,000
You're questioning that we have dreams.

69
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,000
No.

70
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:17,000
But I want to question or ask the experts

71
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:20,000
if there is such a thing as the unconscious.

72
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:24,000
For me, somehow,

73
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:27,000
I don't think it has played any important part

74
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:30,000
in my life at all.

75
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:32,000
Well, it depends on what you mean

76
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,000
by the unconscious.

77
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:34,000
I'll tell you what I mean.

78
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,000
Something hidden,

79
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,000
something incomplete,

80
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:39,000
something that I have to go after

81
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,000
consciously or unconsciously.

82
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
You know, go after and discover it,

83
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:47,000
unearth it, explore it and expose it.

84
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:48,000
Right, right.

85
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,000
See the motives,

86
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:53,000
see the hidden intentions.

87
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,000
Right, right.

88
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Well, could we make it clear, though,

89
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:57,000
that there are some things people do

90
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,000
where you can see they are not aware

91
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:00,000
of what they are doing,

92
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:03,000
but some things of the nature of thought.

93
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:04,000
I don't quite follow.

94
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:07,000
Well, people are...

95
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:08,000
For example, you know,

96
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:10,000
this Freudian slip of the tongue,

97
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:13,000
you know, that somebody makes a slip of the tongue

98
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:15,000
which expresses his real intention, you see.

99
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Oh, yes, yes, yes.

100
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,000
I didn't mean that, quite.

101
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:18,000
I mean, in that sense...

102
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,000
That would be an unconscious.

103
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:22,000
That's what people think of as the unconscious.

104
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:24,000
You see, I think there are two problems

105
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:25,500
here, if I can just

106
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:27,000
put in a technical statement here.

107
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:28,000
There are those people,

108
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:31,000
and there has arisen in the history

109
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,000
of thinking about the unconscious,

110
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,000
people who think that there are...

111
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:37,000
like the unconscious is a thing

112
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:40,000
and that there are things in the unconscious

113
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:43,000
which are there and must be lifted out.

114
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,500
Then I think that there's

115
00:04:44,500 --> 00:04:46,000
a large group of people now

116
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:51,000
who think of the unconscious as areas of behavior

117
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,000
or areas of response

118
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:57,000
or areas of experience that are not...

119
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:00,000
all the connections, we aren't aware,

120
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:03,000
totally aware of all that goes into what happened.

121
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:06,000
So that in the daytime you might have,

122
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:10,000
let's say, an experience of stress

123
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:12,000
or like you would say a disorder.

124
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:14,000
You didn't finish with the experience.

125
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,500
And at night you go

126
00:05:16,500 --> 00:05:19,000
through reworking in a new way.

127
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,000
You have no other way.

128
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,000
So that would be the unconscious

129
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:27,000
and you get other, let's say, from the past

130
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:30,000
or from previous programs of action.

131
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:35,000
I mean, the collective unconscious,

132
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,000
the racial unconscious.

133
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,000
Let's say somebody has been deeply hurt in the past

134
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:40,500
and you can see his

135
00:05:40,500 --> 00:05:42,000
whole behavior is governed by that,

136
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:44,000
though he doesn't know, he may not know it.

137
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:45,000
Yes, that I understand.

138
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,000
His response is always on the basis of the past.

139
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:50,000
Quite.

140
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:53,000
What I'm trying to find out is

141
00:05:53,000 --> 00:06:00,000
why we have divided it,

142
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:03,000
the conscious and the unconscious.

143
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:09,000
Or is it one unitary total process, moving,

144
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:15,000
not hidden, not concealed,

145
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:20,000
but moving as a whole current.

146
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:23,000
And we come along,

147
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:27,000
clever, brainy birds come along

148
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,000
and split it up

149
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:33,000
and say there is the unconscious and the conscious,

150
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,000
the hidden, the incomplete,

151
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:40,000
the storehouse of racial memories,

152
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:43,000
family memories, G, all that.

153
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:46,000
Well, the reason that happened, I think,

154
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:49,000
is that, well, just partially explained,

155
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:52,000
is the fact that Freud and Jung

156
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:54,000
and these people that were seeing patients,

157
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,000
out of which grew so much of the knowledge

158
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:57,000
about the unconscious,

159
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:02,000
would see patients, people who had separated it,

160
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:04,000
in other words, had fragmented off this movement

161
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:05,000
that you're talking about.

162
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,000
That's what I want to get at.

163
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,000
Right.

164
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:11,000
In other words, a woman who says that she is...

165
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:13,000
the whole history of hysteria,

166
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:15,000
you know, where patients couldn't move their arm.

167
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:16,000
I know.

168
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:17,000
You know about that.

169
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:18,000
And then if you open up the memory,

170
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,000
Yes.

171
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,000
for a certain reason,

172
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:22,000
then they eventually can move the arm.

173
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:23,000
So they put two and two together.

174
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:25,000
They don't think it worked that way,

175
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:27,000
but that's the way they did it.

176
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:29,000
Or there were people who had dual personalities.

177
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,000
What I'm trying to...

178
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:33,000
Is it an insanity?

179
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:35,000
Not insanity.

180
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:39,000
Is it a state of mind that divides everything

181
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,000
that says there is the unconscious, conscious?

182
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:44,000
It is a process of fragmentation also.

183
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:45,000
Right.

184
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:48,000
Well, wouldn't you say that certain material

185
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,000
is made...

186
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:50,000
Even Freud has said that certain material

187
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:53,000
is made unconscious by the brain

188
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:55,000
because it's too disturbing.

189
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:56,000
That's what I was...

190
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:57,000
It's fragmented.

191
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:59,000
I mean, that's well known in all forms of psychology.

192
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,000
That's right.

193
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,000
That's what I'm saying.

194
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:02,000
That it's fragmented off,

195
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:05,000
and that then was called the unconscious.

196
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:08,000
What is fragmented is the unconscious.

197
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:10,000
I understand that.

198
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,000
But that meant...

199
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:14,000
Would one say that the brain itself is purposely,

200
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:17,000
or in some sense, holding it separate,

201
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:19,000
to avoid it, you see?

202
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:21,000
Yes, avoid facing the facts.

203
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,000
That's right.

204
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:26,000
Yes, so that it's not really separate from consciousness.

205
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,000
That's what I want to get at, you see?

206
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:29,000
Yes.

207
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:30,000
It is...

208
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,000
Right.

209
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:33,000
I mean, it isn't separate from consciousness.

210
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:36,000
The brain has organised in a fragmented way.

211
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:39,000
Yes, but then it's the wrong terminology to call it...

212
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:42,000
You see, the word unconscious already implies separation.

213
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,000
Separation.

214
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,000
So say there are two layers, for example,

215
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:47,000
the deep unconscious and the surface conscious.

216
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,000
Right, right.

217
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:50,000
That structure is implied.

218
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,000
That's right.

219
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:53,000
But now this other notion is to say there's no...

220
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:56,000
that structure is not implied, but rather certain material,

221
00:08:56,000 --> 00:09:00,000
wherever it may be, is simply avoided.

222
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:01,000
That's right.

223
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:03,000
That's the way I think about it.

224
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:05,000
I don't want to think

225
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,000
about somebody because he's hurting me.

226
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,000
Right.

227
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:09,000
That's not the...

228
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:11,000
It's I don't want to think about it.

229
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:12,000
That's right.

230
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:13,500
I'm conscious, he's hurt me, and

231
00:09:13,500 --> 00:09:15,000
I don't want to think about it.

232
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:17,000
But there's kind of a paradoxical...

233
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:18,500
situation arises because eventually you

234
00:09:18,500 --> 00:09:20,000
become so good at it...

235
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:22,000
that you don't realise you're doing it.

236
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,000
I mean, that seems to happen, you see.

237
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:25,000
Yes, yes, yes.

238
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:28,000
That people become so proficient at avoiding these things...

239
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:30,000
that they cease to realise they're doing it.

240
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:31,000
That's right.

241
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,000
Yes.

242
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:33,000
It becomes habitual.

243
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:34,000
That's right.

244
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,000
I mean, I think this is

245
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:38,000
what happens, that these kinds of things...

246
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:41,000
That is, the wound remains.

247
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:44,000
The wound remains and we forget that we've forgotten.

248
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,000
The wound remains.

249
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:47,000
Right.

250
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:50,000
I suppose we remember to forget this.

251
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:51,000
Yes.

252
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:52,000
We remember to forget.

253
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:55,000
And the process, actually the process of therapy...

254
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:59,000
is helping the remembering, you see, and the recall.

255
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:02,000
To remember you've forgotten...

256
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:07,000
and then to understand the connections of why you forgot...

257
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,500
and then the thing can

258
00:10:08,500 --> 00:10:10,000
move in a more holistic way...

259
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:13,000
rather than being fragmented.

260
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:16,000
Do you consider...

261
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:21,000
or feel that you've been hurt?

262
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,000
Yes.

263
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:25,000
And want to avoid it?

264
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:39,000
Or being hurt, resist, withdraw, isolate...

265
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:42,000
the whole picture, the image

266
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:45,000
of yourself being hurt and withdrawn...

267
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:47,000
all that.

268
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:49,000
Do you feel that when you are hurt?

269
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:50,000
Yes.

270
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:52,000
I feel...

271
00:10:52,000 --> 00:11:00,000
How to put it?

272
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:03,000
I think it's too...

273
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:04,000
I'm interested in this.

274
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Let's go into this.

275
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:09,500
Yes, I feel there is definitely

276
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:13,000
a move not to be hurt...

277
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:14,000
not to be...

278
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,000
not to have that image...

279
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:21,000
not to have that whole thing changed.

280
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:22,000
Because if it's changed...

281
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:24,000
it seems to catapult into that

282
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:26,000
same experience that was the hurt.

283
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,000
See, it may not...

284
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,000
this is hurt...

